The graph of $y=f(x)$ is given below.

On the same set of axes, sketch $y=f(2(x+2))$.

\exfigure{1309_q26_1}

solutions.latex:
\textbf{Original function:} $y=\cos\big(2a(x-b)\big)+c$

\textbf{New function:} $y=-c\sin\big(3a(x-b)\big)$

\begin{itemize}
\item Centre of motion at $c$ corresponds to the amplitude of the new function
\item Both functions have been translated horizontally by $b$
\item Ratio of periods of the original function to the new function: $2a:3a=2:3$. Therefore, the new function will sketch 3 periods within the same time that the original function sketched 2 periods. (i.e. 3 periods in 24 boxes or 1 period in 8 boxes)
\item The new function will be a negative sine curve.
\end{itemize}

